dead	o1_said_dead hover PHANTOM · §FILM_X0 mode=old phantom=281	F: So this is dead code? | M: That is what it said. It was wrong.	F: Last time, the editor learned to say where a thing is set. | M: And to say so when nothing sets it. A phantom. Like this one. | F: So this is dead code? | M: That is what it said. Two hundred and eighty one fields, read but never written. | F: And? | M: It was wrong. This one is alive.
why	card: §FILM_PLAN counts old_phantom=281 revived=130 new_phantom=171	F: How can a lookup be wrong? | M: The files were cut into parts. The index did not read the new form.	F: How can a lookup be wrong? | M: The index reads one pattern. Later, the big files were cut into parts, and a part receives the shared object in a different form. The index never saw what those parts write.
alive	n1_alive written at · n2_jumped same file:line · §FILM_PLAN revived=130 · §FILM_X0 mode=new phantom=171	F: And now? | M: The same line. Written in another file.	F: And now? | M: The same line. Written, in another file. And go to definition lands there. | F: How many came back? | M: One hundred and thirty. One hundred and seventy one remain.
unsure	q1_not_sure PHANTOM? + file:line · q2_the_line assigns the name · §FILM_X0 mode=new untied=11	F: Could it be wrong again? | M: Yes. So it learned a third answer.	F: Could it be wrong again? | M: Yes. So it learned a third answer. Phantom, question mark. It found no writer it can prove. But it names a line that assigns this name. | F: And that line? | M: Here. You read it, and you judge. Eleven fields answer like this.
context	c1_context copied=true beside=1 fields= tags= load=	F: I am new to this file. | M: Ask for its context. One page.	F: I am new to this file. | M: Ask for its context. One page. Its own header, how it reaches a user, the fields it sets, the marks it prints. | F: For an assistant? | M: For you, or for one. It is already copied, ready to paste.
value	v1_no_log · v2_value (a real stamped log of the repo's own generator) · v3_edited	F: What did this line last print? | M: Nothing it can prove, and it says so.	F: This line prints a mark. What did it last print? | M: Nothing it can prove. No stamped log, and it says so. | F: I run it, and save the log. | M: Now the last value, with the log and the version that made it. | F: Then I edit the file. | M: The value is withdrawn. The file changed since the log.
facts	§FILM_MCP tools=7 a1 a2 (the real server, real protocol, no model)	F: And an AI assistant? | M: It may ask the same index. The tool never calls one.	F: And an AI assistant? | M: It may ask the same index, through a small local server. Seven questions, read only, no network. It gets the answer you get. | F: Does the tool call the AI? | M: Never.
limits	§FILM_X0 mode=new untied=11 · CODE_ARCHITECTURE_DESIGN §F.15, §F.16 not-in-v1 · §LENS_REAL_EXTRA stamped=0	F: What is still not done? | M: Eleven fields it cannot decide.	F: What is still not done? | M: Eleven fields it cannot decide. Values need stamped logs, and few exist yet. And it does not yet know who owns a file, or which test proves it.
